// Self-hosted code generation (Phase C of the back-end). Walks the typed AST and
// emits LLVM IR as TEXT — no LLVM library to bind. The oracle is behavioral: the
// emitted .ll, compiled with clang and run, must produce the same exit code/output
// as the C++-built binary (LLVM auto-numbers/folds, so the IR text itself can't be
// matched byte-for-byte). Named SSA temps (%tN) sidestep LLVM's strict 0,1,2,…
// numbering for unnamed values.
//
// S0: functions returning an integer constant.
// S1: scalar locals + params via alloca/load/store, integer arithmetic, comparisons,
//     bitwise ops, unary negate, assignment. Control flow, calls, structs follow.
//
// The module is split into parts, imported here in order (each part relies on the
// declarations of the parts before it, so compile this file, not a part alone):
//   codegen_base.esk       state, target and emission helpers
//   codegen_types.esk      types and layout
//   codegen_ops.esk        operators and conversions
//   codegen_lval.esk       places, calls and builtins
//   codegen_expr.esk       expressions
//   codegen_stmt.esk       statements
//   codegen_decl.esk       functions, lambdas and type declarations
//   codegen_cabi.esk       the C ABI of externs and the program entry

import "codegen_base.esk";
import "codegen_types.esk";
import "codegen_ops.esk";
import "codegen_lval.esk";
import "codegen_expr.esk";
import "codegen_stmt.esk";
import "codegen_decl.esk";
import "codegen_cabi.esk";
